nangate45 picorv32, tpu: drop ABC_CLOCK_PERIOD_IN_PS, which ORFS removed

bazel-orfs carries this against ORFS; it is not upstreamed.

ORFS #4586 removed ABC_CLOCK_PERIOD_IN_PS from variables.yaml (it had
no effect on synthesis) and dropped the gf12 bp_* settings of it, but
nangate45/picorv32 and nangate45/tpu still set it. make ignores an
unknown variable; bazel-orfs refuses one ("Unknown ORFS variable(s) in
arguments"), so both design packages fail to load.

Retires at a bump onto an ORFS whose designs no longer set it.

diff --git a/flow/designs/nangate45/picorv32/config.mk b/flow/designs/nangate45/picorv32/config.mk
--- a/flow/designs/nangate45/picorv32/config.mk
+++ b/flow/designs/nangate45/picorv32/config.mk
@@ -5,7 +5,6 @@
 export SDC_FILE = $(DESIGN_HOME)/$(PLATFORM)/$(DESIGN_NICKNAME)/constraint.sdc
 
 # Synthesis
-export ABC_CLOCK_PERIOD_IN_PS = 900
 export SYNTH_RETIME_MODULES = $(DESIGN_NAME)
 export SYNTH_HDL_FRONTEND = slang
 export LEC_CHECK = 0
diff --git a/flow/designs/nangate45/tpu/config.mk b/flow/designs/nangate45/tpu/config.mk
--- a/flow/designs/nangate45/tpu/config.mk
+++ b/flow/designs/nangate45/tpu/config.mk
@@ -5,7 +5,6 @@
 export SDC_FILE = $(DESIGN_HOME)/$(PLATFORM)/$(DESIGN_NICKNAME)/constraint.sdc
 
 # Synthesis
-export ABC_CLOCK_PERIOD_IN_PS = 1000
 export SYNTH_HDL_FRONTEND = slang
 export LEC_CHECK = 0
 
